-- title:
--   Component intersections occur only at consecutive-chain edge points
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $\mathfrak{X}$ a Deligne–Rapoport model package [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage`](def/ModularCurve_DRModelPackage.html#L43) for $p$, and $O$ a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$; let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ and $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ a ring homomorphism. Assume [`V3Asm.SiteHyps`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L267) for these data, i.e. that the node set $\mathrm{Node}$ — the underlying space of the fibre product of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa$ and $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compZero}\,\kappa$ — is finite, that oriented crossing charts and the étale-neighbourhood and model data exist, and that the marked points $\mathrm{xpt}$ are pairwise distinct and individually closed; assume moreover that each $\xi_j$ lies in the open subscheme `X0` attached to the chart input [`V3Asm.C`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L280), namely the complement of the finite set of marked points. Write $Y$ for the glued scheme, $\mathrm{width}$ for its chain lengths, [`V3Asm.comp`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L404) for the resulting family of ideal sheaf data indexed by chain positions, and [`V3Asm.edgePt`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L410) for the distinguished points. The assertion is: for all distinct chain positions $v \neq w$ and every $y$ in the intersection of the supports of $\mathrm{comp}(v)$ and $\mathrm{comp}(w)$, there are a node $n$ and $d \in \mathrm{Fin}(\mathrm{width}\,n)$ with $y = \mathrm{edgePt}(n,d)$ and $\{v,w\} = \{\mathrm{chainPos}(\mathrm{width},n,d), \mathrm{chainPos}(\mathrm{width},n,d+1)\}$, the two cases of the ordering being given separately. Here $\mathrm{chainPos}$ sends $0$ to the first strict transform, $d$ with $0 < d < \mathrm{width}\,n$ to the $(d-1)$-st exceptional component over $n$, and $d \ge \mathrm{width}\,n$ to the second strict transform.
--
--   This records, for the glued site-level construction, that the components of the special fibre of the resolved Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(p)$ over $O$ meet pairwise only at the singular points of the exceptional chains, and only when the two components are consecutive positions of one and the same chain. It is one of the conditions verified in the existence theorem [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts), which assembles the resolved model together with its crossing charts; the proof invokes the Deligne–Rapoport input that the two strict transforms meet only above the crossings.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_V3Asm_edgePt_exhaust.lean

